   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Azman,<div><br></div><div>To further Hugo&#39;s recommendation, you may find playing around with the mirt::itemplot(shiny=TRUE) interface useful for getting a feel for how/what the supported response models are capable of fitting and how this is reflected in the parameters (and in the classical parameterization transformations for unidimensional models). I generally recommend to those new to the package to get a feel for the IRT models that they are less familiar with first before trying to fit them in practice. HTH.</div><div><br clear=\"all\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Phil</div></div></div></div><br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Thu, Oct 7, 2021 at 10:34 PM Hugo Harada &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">hugo....@adaptativa.com.br</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
